{"id":"mattaniah","name":"Mattaniah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:mattaniah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Mattaniah","text":"Gift of Jehovah. (1.) A Levite, son of Heman, the chief of the ninth class of temple singers (1 Chr. 25:4, 16). (2.) A Levite who assisted in purifying the temple at the reformation under Hezekiah (2 Chr. 29:13). (3.) The original name of Zedekiah (q.v.), the last of the kings of Judah (2 Kings 24:17). He was the third son of Josiah, who fell at Megiddo. He succeeded his nephew Jehoiakin."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4983","lemma":"מַתַּנְיָה","xlit":"Mattanyâh","gloss":"Mattanjah, the name of ten Israelites","kjv":"Mattaniah","count":11,"share":1},{"strong":"H3406","lemma":"יְרִימוֹת","xlit":"Yᵉrîymôwth","gloss":"Jerimoth or Jeremoth, the name of twelve Israelites","kjv":"Jermoth, Jerimoth, and Ramoth","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H2148","lemma":"זְכַרְיָה","xlit":"Zᵉkaryâh","gloss":"Zecarjah, the name of twenty-nine Israelites","kjv":"Zachariah, Zechariah","count":3,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H1131","lemma":"בִּנּוּי","xlit":"Binnûwy","gloss":"Binnui, an Israelite","kjv":"Binnui","count":2,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H3273","lemma":"יְעִיאֵל","xlit":"Yᵉʻîyʼêl","gloss":"Jeiel, the name of six Israelites","kjv":"Jeiel, Jehiel","count":2,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H3881","lemma":"לֵוִיִּי","xlit":"Lêvîyîy","gloss":"a Levite or descendant of Levi","kjv":"Leviite","count":3,"share":0.27}],"verses":["2Kgs.24.17","1Chr.25.4","1Chr.25.16","2Chr.20.14","2Chr.29.13","Ezra.10.26","Ezra.10.27","Ezra.10.30","Ezra.10.37","Neh.12.8","Neh.13.13"],"related":[{"id":"zedekiah","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"jebusites","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.068,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zechariah-zecharias","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.057,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asaph","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.044